Rejig: send gap pins with a layout write so icons placed with empty spaces around them stay
there. Applies to ios_homescreen/state.py, planner.py, model.py and workflow.py from
https://github.com/YakupEmreYerli/ios-homescreen at commit
97649547dbc44295e451c6bf130a87404481e10c, after Rejig's other patches. A layout page may
carry "pins" ({app or web clip id: grid cell 0-23}). The plan keeps them, puts a pinned
page in screen order (SpringBoard reads it back that way), and the write sends them as
listUniqueIdentifiers plus listMetadata fixedLocations, the keys SpringBoard keeps gaps in.
Readback cannot see pins, so a verified write with pins warns that the spots went unchecked.
Pages without pins are sent exactly as before. Method from homescreen-mcp
(https://github.com/kats1123/homescreen-mcp, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Jonathan Kats);
checked on the iOS 26.5 simulator. ios-homescreen is MIT-licensed, Copyright (c) 2026 Yakup
Emre Yerli (full notice in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). This patch is MIT.

